            "summary": "In a 6,000-word blog post on Monday, Burry outlined why he\u2019s now bullish on the government-sponsored enterprises, the political and regulatory hurdles that stand in the way of a public offering, and the steps he says Washington must take before the pair can stage a comeback on Wall Street.  Burry earned a reputation for predicting the collapse of the US housing market before the 2008 financial crisis.  While some investors have famously held Fannie and Freddie positions for over a decade, Burry said he became bullish on the shares only after President Donald Trump\u2019s election last year.",
